Sorry about reopening this, please tell me if it's better to submit another issue.

There is a similar case which still does not work:

```
@QuarkusTest
public class AnnotatedTest {

    @BeforeAll
    public static void beforeAll(TestInfo testInfo) {
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class, testInfo.getTestClass().get());
        Assertions.assertFalse(testInfo.getTestMethod().isPresent());
    }

    @BeforeEach
    public void beforeEach(TestInfo testInfo) throws NoSuchMethodException {
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class, testInfo.getTestClass().get());
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class.getDeclaredMethod("testInfoTestCase", TestInfo.class),
                testInfo.getTestMethod().get());
    }

    @Test
    public void testInfoTestCase(TestInfo testInfo) throws NoSuchMethodException {
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class, testInfo.getTestClass().get());
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class.getDeclaredMethod("testInfoTestCase", TestInfo.class),
                testInfo.getTestMethod().get());
    }

    @AfterEach
    public void afterEach(TestInfo testInfo) throws NoSuchMethodException {
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class, testInfo.getTestClass().get());
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class.getDeclaredMethod("testInfoTestCase", TestInfo.class),
                testInfo.getTestMethod().get());
    }

    @AfterAll
    public static void afterAll(TestInfo testInfo) {
        Assertions.assertEquals(AnnotatedTest.class, testInfo.getTestClass().get());
        Assertions.assertFalse(testInfo.getTestMethod().isPresent());
    }
}

```

In Before/AfterEach the testInfo should return the "Method associated with the current test". In Before/AfterAll it should be an empty optional.

(Also I noticed expected/actual in your PR were inverted.)

